  "groundingSupports": [
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 145,
        "endIndex": 379,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [0]: OpenAI launches \"Astra for Law\"**\n* **Publisher:** openai.com\n* **What is confirmed:** OpenAI officially introduced \"Astra for Law,\" an enterprise platform tailored for legal professionals and software developers"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 381,
        "endIndex": 602,
        "text": "Built on OpenAI's GPT-6 Astra model, it includes a legal search index covering U.S. case law, statutes, regulations, and court decisions (built in partnership with Free Law Project / CourtListener covering over 230M URLs)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 604,
        "endIndex": 758,
        "text": "It also provides 26 ecosystem plugins connecting to tools like Relativity and Clio, with initial integration partners including Harvey, Legora, and Cooley"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 760,
        "endIndex": 838,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** Availability is tailored for enterprise/API customers"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 760,
        "endIndex": 925,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** Availability is tailored for enterprise/API customers; legal reliance still requires human oversight and firm-level compliance configuration"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1039,
        "endIndex": 1199,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [1]: Bug bounty team details exploit chain exposing OpenAI internal repos**\n* **Publisher:** hacktron.ai (also reported by Wall Street Journal)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        2,
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1039,
        "endIndex": 1474,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [1]: Bug bounty team details exploit chain exposing OpenAI internal repos**\n* **Publisher:** hacktron.ai (also reported by Wall Street Journal)\n* **What is confirmed:** Security research firm Hacktron AI published a post-mortem detailing how they chained a heap overflow vulnerability (in `libheif`/`ImageMagick` on OpenAI’s community forum) with an SSO misconfiguration to compromise employee ChatGPT/Codex accounts"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1476,
        "endIndex": 1633,
        "text": "To demonstrate access without reading sensitive code, the researchers submitted Pull Request #1186742 in OpenAI's internal `openai/openai` monorepo on GitHub"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1635,
        "endIndex": 1727,
        "text": "OpenAI patched the vulnerabilities within 72 hours of disclosure and awarded a $6,500 bounty"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1729,
        "endIndex": 1894,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** The security breach occurred in late July 2026 and was responsibly disclosed and fixed prior to the public writeup published on September 18"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2007,
        "endIndex": 2348,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [7]: Anthropic sets up SF Bay Area wet lab for AI life sciences**\n* **Publisher:** Reuters\n* **What is confirmed:** Anthropic’s Head of Life Sciences, Eric Kauderer-Abrams, confirmed to Reuters that the company has established a physical \"wet lab\" in the San Francisco Bay Area to support its AI-driven biological research"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2350,
        "endIndex": 2481,
        "text": "The move follows Anthropic’s acquisition of Coefficient Bio to integrate physical experimental feedback loops into model training"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2483,
        "endIndex": 2739,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** An Anthropic spokesperson clarified that the facility is not designed for direct end-to-end drug discovery itself, but rather to conduct physical biological experiments that validate model predictions alongside third-party partners"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2877,
        "endIndex": 3230,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [8]: Revolut CEO explores dual listing in New York and London**\n* **Publisher:** Financial Times\n* **What is confirmed:** Revolut CEO Nik Storonsky confirmed in an interview with *Les Echos* (and reported by the FT) that the fintech unicorn is actively exploring a dual stock market listing on Nasdaq and the London Stock Exchange (LSE)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        6
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
